{
 "rootCause": "Two earth solids 1 cm apart (above / below the shaft bottom, y = -35.995 / -36.005). Through a cut, the upper solid's bottom is a back face shaded as the cut surface at its own depth (sectionShader.ts FRAGMENT_CAP) and the lower solid's top a lit front face 1 cm under it: closer than the 24-bit depth buffer resolves at the talk's / Explore's distances (near 0.5 m: ~5 mm at 200 m, ~1 cm at 300 m, ~2.4 cm at 450 m). The two z-fought in streaks that crawled as the cut or the camera moved. Also the basemat bottom over the same face.",
 "fix": "scene/plant/materials.ts earthBelowShaft: the lower earth has its own material with polygonOffset (factor 1, units 4), so it always yields in depth to the surfaces 1 cm above it. No geometry, colour, shader or draw-order change.",
 "evidenceForRootCause": "Hiding the lower earth block removed the streaks (diagnosis run); the fix changes pixels only in the excavation where they were (static diffs below) and the 48 s film frames are unchanged.",
